  hintTitle: "Saint-R\xE9my, February 1890"
  lineArrive: A letter from Theo! My hands are shaking. Will you read it to me?
  linePaint: Slowly. Let each one open.
  lineDone: Now I know what to paint for his room.
  hintOpen: Open the window
  hintBrush: Take a brush
  hintFollow: Hold the trigger and follow the branch
  hintSweep: Hold the trigger and brush over the branches
  hintOthers: Wake the other branches
  hintLetter: Take the letter
  hintRead: Pull the trigger to put the letter down
  lineHappy: A boy, and they have named him Vincent! After me. I could not be happier.
  lineInvite: I want to paint it for his room, to hang above his cradle. Will you
    help me? Open the window.
  linePoint: Look, the almond tree outside is just coming into blossom.
  hintDone: "Almond Blossom, Saint-R\xE9my, February 1890"
  letterBackground: "Saint-R\xE9my, February 1890. Vincent has lived in the asylum
    here since last May, painting whenever he is well enough. A letter comes from
    his brother Theo in Paris."
  letterText: 'Paris, 31 January 1890


    My dear Vincent,


    Today Jo gave
    birth to a fine boy, and mother and child are both well. As we promised, we are
    naming him after you: Vincent Willem. I wish that he may be as determined and
    as courageous as you.


    There is good news of your work too: Aurier has written
    about your paintings in the Mercure de France, and your canvases are hanging
    in Brussels with Les Vingt.


    Jo sends you her love.


    Your brother,

    Theo'
  letterReach: 1.8
  letterMinSeconds: 2
  letterMaxSeconds: 25
  happySeconds: 4
  vincentIdleClip: Idle
  vincentGiveClip: Giving
  vincentHappyClip: Happy
  vincentTalkClip: Talking
  vincentRestClip: Idle
  vincentPointClip: Pointing
