  endPaintingSeconds: 2
  endEaselDelay: 7
  lineEasel: Come, look.
  hintTurn: Turn around
  endLookDegrees: 30
  endEpilogueWait: 15
  epilogueTitle: "Almond Blossom, Saint-R\xE9my, February 1890"
  epilogueText: 'Vincent painted these branches of white almond blossom against a
    blue sky as a gift for his newborn nephew. He meant it to hang in Theo and Jo''s
    bedroom; they gave it a place of honour above the piano in their Paris home.


    The
    boy, Vincent Willem van Gogh, grew up to found the Van Gogh Museum in Amsterdam,
    where Almond Blossom hangs today.'
  epilogueCredit: Vincent van Gogh, Almond Blossom, 1890. Van Gogh Museum, Amsterdam
    (Vincent van Gogh Foundation)
